@startuml workspace-transfer
title R-TRANSFER: dispatcher workspace contract and board exact-candidate path (draft)
participant "Original caller principal" as C
participant "Dispatcher\nno repository; journals digests" as D
database "Dispatcher journal\nplan/digests/export obligation" as J
participant "swarma-workspace-materialize\napproved executor; child UID" as M
participant "Worker\nprivate standalone repository" as W
participant "User manager\naccount-wide stop scope" as H
participant "Project-side executor\nservice principal; workplace fence" as F
participant "swarma-workspace-export\napproved executor; child UID; no network" as X
participant "Board change-request machinery\norchestrator executes; formats unpublished" as B
participant "Trusted reviewer\nnot producer; not untrusted" as R
== materialize base B ==
C -> D : admitted base B as bounded canonical tree archive with start
D -> J : archive digest; plan covers B, manifest digest, write scope, exec profile, task-resource digests
D -> M : relay archive; approved child-UID materialization before work
M -> W : standalone private repository; fresh config; no hooks/remotes/credential helpers
M -> W : task resources read-only next to workspace; data, never instructions
note over D,W
  R-UNTRUSTED: workplace untrusted unless operator act admits remote worker to trusted circle.
  Membership enables donor-side opt-ins only; all host boundaries stay.
  Every workplace: no subscription binding or host-local loop.
  R-NET-TOOL/R-EXEC: workplace zero egress; qualified executable whitelist.
  Worker has no push/merge-request access; code leaves only as platform-taken data.
  R-VERIFY: builds/tests/worker code execution only on off-host secret-free runners.
  Web default-off; explicit per-identity trusted-circle opt-in only.
  Worker asks for more resources by letter/outcome and never fetches.
  Archive/plan/resource/transport/retention formats and cap values unpublished.
  Result schema is DRAFT: schemas/workspace-result-1.schema.json (§5.2.1).
end note
W -> W : edit in admitted write scope; platform ignores worker .git/commits/history
== round end and export ==
W -> C : board outcome (local) or signed final envelope (remote)
C -> D : round end (transport unpublished); intermediate export at turn boundary under same fence
D -> J : journal current-execution exec.stop intent; retain export obligation
D -> H : exec.stop; account-wide scope
H --> D : confirmed absence of every account process, or unknown/pending
opt workplace round
  D -> F : write-fence round workspace
  F --> D : refuse further tool calls into this round
end
alt absence or required fence unconfirmed
  break no export or candidate
    D -> J : retain claims/obligation; no export or home deletion
    D --> C : pending/unknown evidence
  end
else absence and required fence confirmed
  D -> J : journal export intent
  D -> X : approved child-UID export with fixed environment, no network
  X -> X : walk without following links; skip .git; compare files to plan manifest
  alt forbidden path/type/collision/submodule/root escape or exceeded cap
    break refused result; no change set or candidate
      X --> D : DRAFT workspace-result/1 refused; reason_class + offending_path; entries empty
      D -> J : journal refusal/result digest; retain export obligation; deletion blocked unless operator waiver
      D --> C : refused workspace-result/1; original caller only; no partial entries or blobs
    end
  else valid bounded change set
    X --> D : DRAFT workspace-result/1 recorded; blob SHA-256/size/mode, link text, deletes
    X --> D : content-addressed blobs; no inline file contents (transport unpublished)
    D -> J : record export/result digests; discharge export obligation
    D --> C : swarma-dispatcher workspace-result/1; original caller only
  end
end
== board-owned import and exact-commit review after valid export ==
C -> B : accept result as resource; deterministic import on B
B -> B : scratch index; no hooks/attribute filters/drivers
B -> B : refuse .git, outside write scope, .task-board; flag sensitive paths and every symlink
B -> B : sign candidate C with repository identity; worker/run/result-digest trailers
B -> B : verify C tree equals recomputed B plus change set
B -> R : review exactly C; execution only in R-VERIFY
R --> B : verdict bound to C (K1); flagged paths acknowledged hunk by hunk
alt changes requested
  B -> C : findings; next admitted base C
  C -> D : next round archive from C; remote signed letter or local task snapshot
  D -> M : materialize fresh workspace from C; remove old round only after recorded export
  M -> W : rework on C; donor-side session continues for remote worker
  W -> W : next fenced round/export produces C2 on C; repeat exact-candidate review
else exact C accepted
  B -> B : signed fast-forward of accepted exact head (K1/K3)
  note right of B : Moved base requires ordinary refresh and re-review.
end
note over D,J
  Export cleanup obligation precedes retirement; only explicit operator act waives it.
  No relaxed home permissions or recursive chown; dispatcher holds no repository.
  Import/candidate/review/integration belong to the board and remain unpublished here.
  Remote-workplace protocol v2.1 sections 8 and 10 gates adopted; executor exports under UID.
end note
legend
  Defining spec: §§3.6, 4.2, 5.2-5.4, 14, 16 question 22.
  workspace-result/1 fields and closed reason classes are explicitly authorized DRAFT (§5.2.1).
  Other design labels do not publish commands, wire fields, refusal codes or cap values.
  Round-end and blob transport remain unpublished (§16 question 22).
endlegend
@enduml
